  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_021: pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) achieves 0.629 acc / 0.599 F1. All six completed multiprofile experiments use concat fusion; weighted fusion has never been tested in the multiprofile setting. Aggregation (avgpool > transformer) and image encoder (vit_l ≥ resnet50) effects are partially characterized, but the fusion strategy remains entirely unexplored at the multiprofile level. Question: Does learned weighted fusion outperform simple concatenation when combining RNA and image representations across multiple profiles? config_002 is identical to config_021 in every dimension except fusion (weighted vs concat), making it a clean single-variable comparison. Why best under budget: It directly tests the highest-priority unexplored design axis on the current best configuration. A positive result would identify a new lever for improvement; a null result would efficiently rule out fusion as a factor, narrowing the search to RNA encoder choice (scgpt, scvi) or other dimensions. No other single experiment isolates as important an untested variable with as minimal confounding."
